course: dictionary
lesson: 6095
title: One word, three meanings: metre
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A metre is a unit of length, a way to measure how long, wide or high something is. «The hyacinth macaw is about a metre long from beak to tail.» A big step is roughly one metre, so you can picture it in your head.
explain: Context tells you which meaning is meant. «The parking meter ran out, so Mum put in more coins.» Here a meter is a machine that measures something, not a length. Ask yourself: is this talking about how long something is, a machine, or a beat in a poem?
explain: Metre can also mean the beat in a poem or a song, the regular pattern of strong and weak sounds. In American English, the length unit is spelled meter too, so meter can mean either a unit of length or a machine. Check the words around it and you will know.
fact: A metre is 100 centimetres.
fact: A kilometre is 1000 metres.
fact: «Darwin's bark spider spins webs across rivers up to about 25 metres wide.»
fact: «The narwhal's tusk grows up to about 3 metres long.»
fact: Phrases you will meet: «metres long», «metres wide», «metres high», «square metre», «per metre».
exercise: «The hyacinth macaw is about a metre long from beak to tail.» How long is a metre? | About the height of a house | *About the length of a big step | The weight of a schoolbag | A tiny pencil
exercise: «The parking meter ran out, so Mum put in more coins.» What is a meter here? | A beat in a poem | *A machine that measures something | A unit of length | A kind of bird
exercise: «Ukraine's black earth is about a metre deep.» What does metre measure here? | *How far down the earth goes | How fast the soil moves | Weight of the soil | Heat
test: How many centimetres are in one metre? | 10 | *100 | 1000 | 50
test: Ruby says, «The poem's metre is strong: da-DUM, da-DUM.» What is metre in this line? | A machine | A kind of tree | *The beat in a poem | A measure of length
exam: How many metres are in 2 kilometres? | 20000 | 20 | 200 | *2000
